FINDINGS (for antigravity chat A1; I report, I do not fix)

F1 (blocking under rule 15). E4-P1 is MISSED and it breaks the claimed invariant:
   with the verdict comparison gone, a Failed verdict with complete parameters is
   stored. test_add_math_case_with_unverified_verdicts_refused passes for the
   wrong reason, because its four evidence dicts also fail the points_tested and
   max_relative_error checks. Fix in novacore/tests/test_casememory.py: give each
   unverified verdict a complete, otherwise storable payload, and keep one case
   per verdict so the assertion names the verdict. Then E4-P1 goes red.

F2 (blocking under rule 15). E4-P4 is MISSED: the maths detector has one test of
   implicit detection, and that test matches on the "x^2" branch, so any keyword
   can be deleted from _MATH_PATTERNS without a test noticing. With
   "differentiate" gone, "Differentiate 4t cubed with respect to t" is stored as
   a general case with no evidence. Fix: a table-driven test that, for every
   keyword in _MATH_PATTERNS, feeds a question containing only that keyword and
   asserts CaseVerificationError without evidence. Build the table from the
   pattern itself is not enough (that is the code grading itself); write one
   literal question per keyword, or read the keyword list from a small
   hand-written JSON fixture.

F3 (low, not blocking). E4-P3 is MISSED but the chain hash catches the same
   tampering, so no data can be altered undetected (section 4). The content_sha256
   check duplicates the chain check for a single record. Either give it its own
   test (recompute content_sha256 so only the chain check can fire, the mirror of
   test_tampered_chain_hash_detected) or delete it and say the chain is the check.

F4 (low). The false-replay measurement is printed but not bounded:
   test_paraphrase_fixture_evaluation_and_false_replay_rate asserts only
   assertGreater(true_positives, 0), assertGreater(true_negatives, 0) and
   assertIsInstance(false_replay_rate, float). A regression that replays every
   query would keep the suite green while printing 100%. The commit message
   claims "Measured false-replay rate 33.33% without artificial threshold
   tuning". Measuring is not a claim I can falsify, so this is not blocking; pin
   the measured values (5 TP, 2 FP, 4 TN, 2 FN at threshold 0.8) so the fixture
   becomes a regression test.

F5 (cosmetic). Commit eaf1bff's subject begins with a UTF-8 BOM (U+FEFF), which
   shows in git log --oneline as "﻿e4: ...". Same pattern as 8fdba63 and 0353f6e.
   No action from me; worth avoiding in future commits.

VERDICT: FAIL
  E4-P2 (anchor check) is CAUGHT, so the tamper-evident tail has teeth. E4-P1
  (verdict gate) and E4-P4 (maths detector) are MISSED and each lets an
  unverified maths answer into the permanent log with all 12 tests green, which
  is the AGENTS.md invariant "nothing unverified becomes permanent" broken by a
  one-line change. E4-P3 is MISSED but redundant with the chain check. Two
  blocking test gaps, both in A1's file; the production code is correct today.
